On the twenty-fifth day of my internship, I started studying users 
and groups in Linux. I read the related sections from the Linux book 
and learned how Linux manages different users and groups on a system.

I studied commands such as whoami, id, and groups and learned how 
they can be used to obtain information about the current user and 
group memberships. I also reviewed the /etc/passwd and /etc/group 
files to understand where basic user and group information is stored.

I connected these topics with the file permission concepts that 
I had learned previously. Understanding users, groups, and 
permissions helped me see how Linux controls access to files 
and system resources.
